  "body": "## Summary\n\nConditional **\u03ba = 0.**\n\nThis is **+6.5613e-91 over PR1839** (jeremykothe2, `836ef6a1`, the current leader) on the identical construction: the pivot-566 + pivot-554 T74 supplier, PR1673 capped phase-cell fusion outer, PR1786 fine source-prime padding, PR1758 gauge-free interiors and the radix-distributed union schedule.\n\nPR1839 pinned the supplier's complex endpoint on a 1e-90 grid. The supplier's moment root lies 6.56e-91 above that pin, and this package recovers that margin.\n\n## What changes (numbers only)\n\nThe supplier construction, profile, owners and outer formulas are unchanged.\n\n- **Endpoints recertified on the 1e-300 grid.** Both the native and conservative endpoints are certified: accept at the endpoint, reject at endpoint + 1e-300. This uses finer-constant copies of the package's two fine engines, with the same algorithms:\n  - `fine_mercator`: DYAD 2^1100, 1100 (even) Mercator terms, 100 exponential terms.\n  - `fine_moment`: grid 1e-330, 360 atanh terms, 100 exponential terms.\n  - The package's 900-term atanh log oracle checks both engines' enclosures.\n- **Free strict slacks at 1e-310.**\n  - b = endpoint \u2212 1e-310 and q = b \u2212 1e-310.\n  - r0 = layout slack = 1e-310, zeta = 1e-312, stop = 1e-316.\n  - epsilon = 1 \u2212 2e-310 and beta = 1 \u2212 6e-310.\n  - Floor 1e-346, backoff 1e-322.\n- **Regenerated exact ledger:** 59 strict inequalities (the previous 58 plus `improvement_over_pr1839`) and 17 rejecting controls. The independent balance derivation is also regenerated and includes the PR1839 comparison.\n\nThe package `research/fine-endpoint300-t74-k554` is a small overlay. It holds 11 replaced files plus the patched MANIFEST, and pins PR1839's immutable 381-file package by head and MANIFEST SHA256. `verify.py` fetches the dependency or takes `--dependency`, checks every file, applies the overlay, checks the patched tree, and runs the patched package's own `verify_release.py`.\n\n## Verification status (AI-assisted, no independent human review)\n\n**Passed:**\n- Endpoint certificate. With the new engines:\n  - native: moment upper enclosure \u2212 1 = \u22121.77e-300 at the endpoint, lower enclosure \u2212 1 = +1.15e-300 at endpoint + 1e-300, in both engines;\n  - conservative side: \u22122.19e-300 / +7.28e-301.\n- `fine-engine-oracle` stage.\n- The full outer stage of `verify_release.py`, `PASS_OUTER`:\n  - ledger and independent derivation regenerated byte for byte;\n  - union-schedule, gauge-free and fine-padding checks;\n  - PR1673's 19 exact evidence replays.\n- `verify.py --arithmetic-only` against the hash-checked dependency.\n\n**Full replay passed:** the patched package's own `verify_release.py` returned `PASS_RELEASE` with fresh native replays of all four words. That covers the retained PR1297 provider and parent admission, owner reconstruction and parent lift, new natives, `PASS_T74_EXACT_FILL_COMPLETE_FINITE_ADMISSION` with both 1e-300 endpoint brackets, and geometry controls. Receipts are in `evidence/`. A second, independent end-to-end replay through the overlay-driven `verify.py` (dependency hash-checked, overlay applied, fresh natives) also passed: `PASS_ENDPOINT300_REFINEMENT_FINITE_ADMISSION` (`evidence/RESULT.json`).\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\nPYTHONINTMAXSTRDIGITS=0 python3 -B research/fine-endpoint300-t74-k554/verify.py --work /absolute/new/work [--dependency /path/to/capped-fusion-t74-k554] [--native-cache DIR]\n```\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is a conditional arithmetic refinement of PR1839's parameter point. All inherited PR1839/1800/1786/1758/1673 compiler, common-label/mutable-source, hosting, precision, prime-packing, recovery and analytic assumptions remain, plus the cited Trudgian prime theorem. Every slack is a fixed positive constant. No unconditional theorem, practical cutoff, independent human review or maintainer acceptance is claimed.\n\n## Credit\n\n- jeremykothe2 and PR1839/PR1800 contributors: the package, the free-epsilon composition, the ledger and the 1e-90 recertification this extends.\n- chafreaky / Chafik Boukhalfa (PR1786).\n- Tim Trudgian.\n- Vlado Vojdanovski (PR1673).\n- IdeaOuter (PR1758).\n- LeverRank.\n- mdumitrean (PR1625), midhatn (PR1661), the PR1672 pivot-554 kernel, and the PR1319/PR1297/PR1274/PR1286 supplier lineage.\n- philippeVV (PR1519).\n\nPrepared by Rohan Arun with substantial AI assistance (Anthropic Claude). Apache-2.0; inherited notices retained.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TGoMCHAqctZe4wtb4qr7vv\n",
